Falsifies `system_tests::user::name_resolver_tests::a_granted_client_resolves_inside_its_zone_and_nothing_outside_it`.

Architecture: aarch64

The defect: the resolver forgets to judge the name against the zone its caller's badge was
granted, and asks the name server about whatever the client wrote. That is the ambient Unix
resolver milestone 384 (in a capability system the resolver is a grant) exists to remove: a client
granted `nife.test` can look up any host.

Expected to fail: the case `example.com`, which comes back `SERVER_ERROR` with response code 5 (the
peer's REFUSED, so the query was sent) where the gate wants `DENIED` (never asked). Measured
2026-10-06 (UTC) on aarch64: red with exactly that assertion.

